%S A400888 2,2,1,2,2,1,1,2,1,2,6,1,2,1,1,2,1,1,1,2,1,2,4,1,1,2,1,1,20,1,11,2,2,
%T A400888 1,2,1,62,15,1,2,14,1,8,6,1,2,10,1,2,1,1,2,6,1,3,1,1,14,3,1,2,5,2,2,1,
%U A400888 2,1,1,1,2,1,1,1,2,2,1,1,1,1,2,1,2,2,1,4,38,2,2,3,1,1,4,1,2,6,1
%N A400888 Contents of the quarter-turn corrected Stern vectors associated with the column words of the Gosper-Lafitte triangle.
%C A400888 Let V(n) be the filled-empty word in column n of the fractal set described in A000360, considered from the narrow top downward, with filled=1 and empty=0. V(n) is A000361's W(n) read in reverse order. Let f_n=A000360(n) and e_n=A284556(n+1) be its numbers of 1s and 0s. Starting with (p,q)=(1,1), read V(n), replacing (p,q) by (p+q,q) after a 1 and by (p,p+q) after a 0. Let (p_n, q_n) be the resulting Stern vector.
%C A400888 With v_n=(p_n,q_n)^T, c_n=(f_n,e_n)^T, J={{0,-1},{1,0}}, and u_n=v_n + J*c_n, we have a(n) = max {m >= 1 : u_n == (0,0)^T (mod m)}.
%C A400888 Consequently V(n) determines both an order-sensitive Stern vector and its commutative Parikh vector; a(n) is the content of u_n, meaning the gcd of its coordinates.
%C A400888 For r >= 0, V(3*2^r - 2) consists of r+1 zeros followed by r ones.
%C A400888 Every positive integer divides some term of this unbounded sequence. Every positive even integer occurs infinitely often as a term. It is conjectured that the sequence is surjective onto the positive integers.
%D A400888 M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas), Sur l'Effet Noah en Géometrie, rapport à l'INPI, Mars 1995.
%H A400888 M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas), <a href="/A400888/b400888.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..9999</a>
%F A400888 a(n) = gcd(p_n - e_n, q_n + f_n), with (p_n, q_n) and (f_n, e_n) as defined above.
%F A400888 a(4^j*(n+1) - 1) = a(n), for j,n >= 0.
%F A400888 a(3*2^r - 2) = (r+1)*gcd(r,2), for r >= 0.
%F A400888 a(3*2^(6*k+2) - 2^(2*k) - 1) = 8*k + 6, for k >= 0.
%e A400888 V(22)={0,0,0,0,1,1,1}. Its Stern vector is (p_22,q_22)=(16,5), while (f_22,e_22)=(3,4). Hence, (p_22 - e_22, q_22 + f_22)=(12,8), and the gcd is 4=a(22).
%o A400888 (PARI)
%o A400888 f(v, c, h=0) = [2*(x + h) + c - (2*c + 1)*(x%2) | x <- v];
%o A400888 w(n) = {my(m = n\2); if(n < 1, if(n, [], [1]), if(n%2, f(w(m), m%3 != 2, 1), concat(f(w(m), m%3 != 0), f(w(m - 1), m%3 != 2))))};
%o A400888 a(n) = {my(v = vecsort(w(n),,4), p = 1, q = 1, ones, zeros); ones = sum(i = 1, #v, v[i]%2); zeros = #v - ones; for(i = 1, #v, if(v[i]%2, p += q, q += p)); gcd(p - zeros, q + ones)};
%o A400888 vector(96, n, a(n - 1))
%Y A400888 Cf. A000360 and A284556 for the filled and empty column counts, A000361 for the binary encodings of the column words, and A002487 for the total column lengths and the Stern enumeration of the positive rationals underlying the obtention of (p_n,q_n).
%K A400888 nonn,eigen,new
%O A400888 0,1
%A A400888 _M. Jeremie Lafitte (Levitas)_, Oct 08 2026
